# Mutators whose value #2022's gate cannot show travels in the state blob.
#
# Read by src/doppler/tests/test_mutator_state.py: every serializable
# object's post-create mutators, found from objects/*.toml and the C headers,
# probed by behaviour. A mutator that does not pass (TRAVELS or KEYED) must be
# listed here with EXACTLY the verdict it reads and a reason, or the gate is
# red. A listed mutator that now passes, names nothing, or reads another
# verdict is red too: this list only shrinks. The rule is
# docs/design/state-serialization.md, "A mutator's value is state".
#
#   LOST              its value does not travel: a fix deletes the line
#   NONDETERMINISTIC  two identical builds differ, so no restore can be judged
#   UNPROBED          no two values the probe can find differ (reason: why)
#   EXEMPT            a handle to the outside world, not state
#   C_ONLY            no Python face to probe: verified by a C twin, #2077
#   NO_RECIPE         its class has no CASES row to probe with, #2078
#
# Each family's fix PR deletes its own lines (#2079..#2084, LO/NCO first).
#
# key                                                    verdict           reason

# -- LOST (15)
